{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1020276-2e-fan-cult-of-the-doomsday-clock","id":1020276,"title":"[2E Fan] Cult of the Doomsday Clock","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T04:33:49-08:00","id":1020276,"title":"[2E Fan] Cult of the Doomsday Clock","content":"As I wanted to return with Cult of the Doomsday Clock to my game, here is update of them to 2E rules. If you want to read more about their changes in 2E and usage of Legacy in my London game \u2013 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/559433-2ed-cult-of-doomsday-clock\">see here</a>. I\u2019m still not sure if they still strive for entering Supernal World, when every mage can do this with Focused Mage Sight. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Cult of the Doomsday Clock</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Moros ( but recruit any Path members, especially Acanthus )<br /> <b>Appearance &amp; Background</b>: In <b>Legacies: The Sublime</b>, page 128.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 2, Occult or Science 1<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Future Cult member must find Legacies teacher and give him his Sympathy Name, blood and hair to be locked in initiates Doomsday Clock.<br /> <b>Organization:</b> : In <b>Legacies: The Sublime</b>, page 128. Foliots are Initiates in Legacy, Hands are those that got to Second Attainment. Tollers are those that archived Third Attainment. Anachrons are those that got Fourth Attainment. Horea are masters of Legacy, getting Fifth Attainment.<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Tick-Tock<br /> <b>Theory:</b> This Fallen World is only one of many. Other \u2018unborn\u2019 realities are in Abyss. If we end this one with correct version of world in mind, we will change the world! Or free our souls from eternal torment, straight to Supernal World. Either way, we must strive for Great End of this world.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Magic</span></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Time<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Casting in the presence of temporal distortion (+1, +2 when trying to analyze or stem the phenomenon itself), erasing object from Time ( +2, need to cast Erase History on item ).<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> In <b>Legacies: The Sublime</b>, page 129.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Attainments</span></b><br /> <b>First:</b> <i>Wrong Time</i><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> The mage can detect time distortions and manipulations, as with an active version of Time Arcanum Mage Sight, even without activating it. He can detect when someone has altered the temporal timeline of an area (for example, moving objects back or forward in time), or the place is one of the Abyssal. This power activates automatically whenever the Tick-Tock encounters an anomaly of this kind and allows to discern it using only Peripheral Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: </b>Death 1<br /> Everything has the end and Tick-Tock can sense when it comes to things he sees. He just need made 1 tur of concentration on target and will get a sense when object he is watching will perish.<br /> <br /> <b>Second:</b> <i>Stopping Time</i><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 2, Occult or Science 2<br /> Tick-Tock can froze things in Time, so they will be preserved for coming end of Fallen World as we know it, without alterations of other parties. Works as <i>Constant Presence</i> spell with Duration in his dots of Time.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Death 2<br /> The final destination of world is it\u2019s end, so mage faster it a bit. It works as <i>Decay</i>, with mage dots in Death as Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Third:</b> <i>Bid Time Return</i><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 3, Occult or Science 2<br /> Tick-tocks want the world to be in state of their vision before it\u2019s ended. To get this, you need to choose best version of events. To get this, Cult members can use this Attainment. It works as <i>Shifting Sands</i> spell, with Potency high as his Time dots and cost one Mana per each usage.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Death 3<br /> If a Tick-Tock also possesses Death 3, his ability to <i>Bid Time Return </i>is not limited by death. If circumstances lead to his immediate death, he automatically bounces back a turn. Unlike <i>Shifting Sands </i>alone, the damage that killed the character also reverses, so he\u2019s alive again and can try to avoid his doom. If no possible action can save him, he must experience his death over and over \u2014 at least until he runs out of Mana or gives up.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth:</b> <i>Other Time\u2019s End</i><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 4, Occult or Science 3<br /> The Tick-Tock can change subject timeline to prepare it for the Great End. It works as <i>Rewrite History, </i>with mage Time dots as Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Death 4<br /> The Tick-Tock can lead subject straight to his Great End. It works as <i>Withering </i>spell, with Potency equal to his Death dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth:</b> <i>Off The Clock</i><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Time 5, Occult or Science 4<br /> The Tick-Tock can now slip between normal timeline and hyperpacked time, doing everything he need for the Great End to prepare. Works as <i>Blink of an Eye</i>, with mage Time dots as Potency. By spending Mana he can use Reach option for spellcasting, once per each Mana point spent.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Death 5<br /> The final trick of Tick-Tock is to simply end existence of things. At Death 5 he can made things to be dead for the world \u2013 it works as <i>Empty Presence</i> spell. With powers of Time erasing on it, target is almost impossible to be brought back from dead, ended on multiple levels.<br /> <br /> New Spell: <i>Erase History </i>( Time 4 )<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency vs. Temporal Sympathy<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Weaponry, Stealth, Intimidation<br /> Mage <i>destroys</i> part of subjects Temporal timeline to be perceived by Time Arcanum and related phenomena. Target <b>was</b> having actions destroyed before, but for any Time senses, he <i>does not exist</i> in affected time. Duration Factor determines how much of Time can be erased by the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-21-2016, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}